    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Af612NXHPWxT94cRQErVvq)_\n\n- `sp-search.el` (in `base/navi/`) had one `)` too many on the `ag` entry of `sp-search-menu`: `(fboundp 'ag))))]` is now `(fboundp 'ag)))]`.\n- `sp-navi` requires `sp-search`, so the `invalid-read-syntax` stopped `sp-navi` from loading.\n- Fixed in the doc (`docs/tangles/custom/sp-search-browsing-trails.org`) and the `.el` together; `tools/check-tangle.sh` matches once both are committed.\n- `sp-faces.el` in the repo is fine (reads and tangles cleanly). Sia's local copy has leftover `git stash` conflict markers (`<<<<<<< Updated upstream` ... `>>>>>>> Stashed changes`) that are not in git; see the thread.\n- No CHANGELOG edits.\n\nChecked by reading every form of the file with Emacs 29.3 in batch; not loaded in a full session.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCp95tyuooQzbQy3uw)_",
